  "id": "Compound::DB00656 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Trazodone is implicated in the regulation of Cyp2d6 through a chain of interactions involving taste disturbances. The evidence suggests that Trazodone causes taste peculiarities, which are then mediated by compounds like Protriptyline, Trimipramine, or Desipramine, all of which bind to Cyp2d6. These compounds are classified as antidepressants and belong to the organonitrogen heterocyclic class, highlighting a potential link between Trazodone and Cyp2d6 through the shared pharmacological profile of antidepressant agents. The integration of these pathways underscores a possible mechanism by which Trazodone influences Cyp2d6 activity, likely through the indirect effects of its metabolites or related compounds. The recurring association with antidepressants and heterocyclic structures suggests a broader pharmacological context, though the exact mechanism of Cyp2d6 regulation remains to be fully elucidated.",
